		continue the action;
	say "I'd need my [as a noun]ladder[end as] for that!"

Instead of going up in Rickety Stair:
	say "I scramble up the [as a noun]ladder[end as]. It's a long way, and pretty exhausting.";
	move the player to the Attic Room;


Section 1 - Taking

Instead of taking the caretaker's ladder when the Herb Garden is unvisited:
	say "[one of]Sure. Wandering around with a twelve foot [as a noun]ladder[end as] is going to help me slip through the [as a noun]Abbey[end as] unnoticed.[or]I think [as a noun]Drake[end as] might catch me, stuck in an archway somewhere.[or]How is a ladder going to help me get past [as a noun]Calvin[end as]?[stopping]";

