Instead of taking or pulling or pushing the kettle:
	say "The [as a noun]kettle[end as] is a fixed part of the machine, built into place underneath the [as a noun]spigot[end as]."

Chapter 4 - Burner

The burner is an internal gubbin, part of the tea-machine.
The description is "The [as a noun]burner[end as] is a little [as a noun]spout[end as] for the gas which is pumped in from the cow-sheds in the countryside, or so [as a noun]Drake[end as] says. It's currently unlit but on one side is the [as a noun]flint-iron[end as], ready to spark should the [as a noun]gear-train[end as] connected to it be put in motion."

