Chapter 8 - Gear Train

Section 1 - Description

The gear train is part of the tea-machine.

The description is "[if the tea-machine is switched on]The [as a noun]gears[end as] are whirring quite happily.[otherwise if the new gear is part of the gear train]The [as a noun]gear train[end as] forms a perfect snake from the lever, over the semi-circular [as a noun]bracket[end as] and into the innards of the machine.[otherwise if the small gear is part of the gear train][one of]I can't help but notice [as the small gear]a worn down gear[end as] in the middle of the [as a noun]train[end as], no longer catching teeth with its fellows. I make the sign of Sad Depreciation.[or]One [as the small gear]small central gear[end as] is too worn to mesh with the others. 'The weak ones removed and replaced by better,' [as a noun]Gubbler[end as] might intone.[stopping][otherwise]The [as a noun]gear train[end as] is most sadly broken by the lack of one small cog. If the [as a noun]Cook[end as] sees this, he'll get very upset.[end if]"

