Part 3 - Buttress

Chapter 1 - Description

After going from the Parapet to the Buttress:
	say "I hurl myself in pursuit!";
	continue the action;

Buttress is a room, exterior, west of Parapet. "I'm not on the [as a noun]roof[end as] anymore: I'm perched on a narrow stone arch that curves out from the wall and down to the ground. Hopefully I'm not going <Italic>that</Italic> way any time soon... This is where I saw the [as a noun]Figure[end as] jump across to the next roof, though now he's disappeared from sight." 

Instead of making to leave in the Buttress:
	try going east.

Instead of going east in Buttress:
	say "Back off? No way. I've gotten this far. I'm not giving up.";

Instead of going nowhere when in the Buttress:
	say "There's no way off this [as a noun]buttress[end as] apart from jumping, or falling.";

Instead of falling when in the Buttress:
	say "After I survived that clock in there? That wouldn't just be clumsy, it'd be <Italic>embarrassing</Italic>."

Instead of jumping when in the Buttress:
	say "Heart in mouth? Check. Fingers ready to claw the [as a noun]roof[end as]? Ready. Then – here goes![paragraph break]I spring like a cat – like a <Italic>flying</Italic> squirrel – like a mouse hit out of the kitchen by the [as a noun]Cook[end as] wielding a meat-tenderizer – I hurl myself across the gap and thump down on to the [as a noun]roof[end as] beyond. Good thing this is a Council building: they make their [as a noun]roof[end as]s good and firm.";
	move the player to Rooftop 1;

Instead of approaching the escaping Figure when in the Buttress:
	try jumping.

