Section 2 - Elongated chimney pipe

The elongated chimney pipe is a pointer, hot air vent, fixed in place. "On one side of the [as a noun]roof[end as] is my odd contraption; a bent metal [as a noun]pipe[end as] attached to the [as a noun]iron chimney[end as]. It's belching [as a noun]smoke[end as] and [as a noun]steam[end as] in a generally [way of the item described]erly direction[if the way of the item described is southwest], across the alleyway[end if][if wrapped]. Wrapped around the near end is the [as a noun]sheet[end as] of [as a noun]tarpaulin[end as][end if]."

The description is "My odd construction: the [as a noun]chimney[end as], connected to a long metal [as a noun]pipe[end as], that extends out about ten feet [if the way of the item described is not southwest]across the [as a noun]rooftop[end as] to the [way of the item described][otherwise]over the [as a noun]alley[end as] to the southwest[end if][if wrapped]. Wrapped around the near end is the [as a noun]sheet[end as] of [as a noun]tarpaulin[end as][end if]."

Understand "squat", "iron", "smoke", "slugs", "steam", "hot air" as the elongated chimney pipe.

Understand "curious", "bit", "long", "ten foot", "ten feet", "gigantic", "staple", "length", "piping" as the elongated chimney pipe.

The elongated chimney pipe can be wrapped or unwrapped. The elongated chimney pipe is unwrapped.

The way of the elongated chimney pipe is north.

