Section 3 - Glass Doors

Some glass doors are a door, open, not openable, eyeable, scenery, north of the Grand Foyer, south of the Main Platform. 

Rule for printing the description of the glass doors when the location is the Grand Foyer:
	say "Beyond the [as a noun]glass doors[end as] is the complex and intricate machine, its pinions bent by the warped glass into meaningless shapes[if the Calculatrix Pristina is in the Main Platform]. In front of the machine I can make out two [as a noun]ladies[end as], one [as a noun]short[end as] and [as a noun]dark-haired[end as] wearing a [as a noun]long white gown[end as], the other [as a noun]elegant[end as], [as a noun]thin[end as] and dressed up like a princess at a ball[end if]."

Rule for printing the description of the glass doors when the location is the Main Platform:
	say "The [as a noun]glass doors[end as] lead back - and obscure my view of - the Grand Foyer."

Does the player mean doing something with the glass doors: it is likely.

Before going through the glass doors when the location is the Grand Foyer and the Calculatrix Pristina is in the Main Platform and CAL_SPOTTED is unfired:
	fire CAL_SPOTTED instead;

Instead of examining or searching the glass doors when the location is the Grand Foyer and the Calculatrix Pristina is in the Main Platform and CAL_SPOTTED is unfired:
	fire CAL_SPOTTED;

Instead of going through the glass doors from the Grand Foyer when the Calculatrix Pristina is in the Main Platform:
	say "I don't want to get caught and even if the two [as a noun]women[end as] behind the door don't see me they'd be bound to <Italic>smell</Italic> me if I went inside.";

CAL_SPOTTED is a trigger. 

Rule for firing CAL_SPOTTED:
	say "My hand freezes on the door-handle as I overhear a [as a noun]woman[end as]'s voice. 'The [as a noun]machine[end as] works quickly.' Peering through the door I can make out two [as a noun]figures[end as] on the other side, their bodies stretched and bent by the warps in the glass."

After going through the glass doors from the Grand Foyer:
	say "I slip through the [as a noun]glass doors[end as], between the first blocks of the enormous machine and up onto the central platform.";
	continue the action;

Instead of opening the glass doors:
	try entering the glass doors;

Instead of attacking the glass doors:
	say "I'm not here to damage anything - I just need to find out where the [as a noun]Figure[end as] is, and go!"

Understand "beveled/bevelled", "bubbled", "warped", "bubbles", "warps", "door" as the glass doors.

