Rule for choosing the conversation table of Covalt when the second-state of Covalt is 1 during Return to Covalt's:
	change the chosen conversation table to the table of concerned Covalt conversation;

CT_COV_R1_MYSELF is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I should tell you what happened, I’ve got to,' I begin hurriedly. 'The [as a noun]Figure[end as], and I found… and there was this [as a noun]rope[end as] and I…'". The response text is "'Slow down, slow down!' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] chides. 'Start with something and go on from there. Or you won’t have a story, you’ll have a coughing fit!'".
CT_COV_R1_BALLOON is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I’m sorry about your [as a noun]skylight[end as].'". The response text is "'Never mind my [as a noun]skylight[end as],' he answers, crossly. 'I don’t want no sorries from half-dead children!'".
CT_COV_R1_ABBEY is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Perhaps I should go back to the [as a noun]Abbey[end as].'". The response text is "'Not until you’ve told me what’s happened to you,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] replies severely.".
CT_COV_R1_CATHEDRAL is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I’ve got to get to the [as a noun]Cathedral[end as],' I insist.". The response text is "'Not till we have a plan you don’t.' He waves the [as a noun]Figure[end as]’s note meaningfully. 'And we won’t have a plan till you’ve told me what’s going on.'".
CT_COV_R1_ABBOT is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'The [as a noun]Abbot[end as] must know I’m missing by now.'". The response text is "'Well, perhaps he cares or not, never mind,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] replies roughly. 'But you’ve been blacked out hard enough that you’re owed a little time without a whipping.'".
CT_COV_R1_FIGURE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'The [as a noun]Figure[end as] must have brought me here,' I say. 'He tried to strangle me…'". The response text is "'So?' [as a noun]Covalt[end as]’s voice is urgent. 'Where were you? What did you find?'".
CT_COV_R1_ARCHBISHOP is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I’ve got to tell the [as a noun]Archbishop[end as]!' I insist.". The response text is "'No you don’t, urchin.' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] stamps his foot. 'You’ve got to tell me.'".
CT_COV_R1_PEOPLE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "He wouldn’t know them.".
CT_COV_R1_COVALT is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Are you all right?' I ask.". The response text is "'Me? ME?' He looks furious. 'I’ve got this half-dead half-guttered gutter rat stinking of river water dropped dead on my doorstep and… oh!' He growls. 'You tell me about you. And leave me out of it, right?'".
CT_COV_R1_RAVENS is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Are your [as a noun]birds[end as] all right?'". The response text is "'You must be addled,' he replies, in a voice as soft as falling granite. 'Worrying about my [as a noun]birds[end as]. Now what happened to you?'".
CT_COV_R1_CLOCKWORK is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I found clockwork,' I begin. 'Clockwork…'". The response text is "'Start from somewhere else,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] insists. 'From the start or wherever but somewhere with sense!'".
CT_COV_R1_PERPETUUM	 is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'He might have stolen the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] already!'". The response text is "'That he might,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] replies. 'But I didn’t feel any earthquake yet and you believe me, if your [as a noun]Figure[end as] starts taking that thing apart you’ll feel it in the wind-up of your bones.'".
CT_COV_R1_DIFFERENCEENGINE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I got to the [as a noun]Engine[end as], like you said,' I tell him.". The response text is "'Course you did,' he replies, with clear pride. 'And where did it send you on to?'".
CT_COV_R1_ARMY is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'The [as a noun]Engine[end as] sent me to the docks!' I tell him. 'And I found – an [as a noun]army[end as]…' I try to describe the [as a noun]soldiers[end as] with their [as a noun]metal faces[end as] and [as a noun]mechanical chests[end as].". The response text is "[as a noun]Covalt[end as] is nodding before I’ve finished. 'So that’s your answer then,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] says, seriously. 'The [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as].'".
CT_COV_R1_NOTE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'You found a [as a noun]note[end as] with me?' I ask, puzzled.". The response text is "'Tucked under your arm. Not a nice note, neither,' he replies.".

CT_COV_R1_MYSELF is clustered with CT_COV_R1_BALLOON, CT_COV_R1_ABBEY, CT_COV_R1_CATHEDRAL, CT_COV_R1_ABBOT, CT_COV_R1_FIGURE, CT_COV_R1_ARCHBISHOP, CT_COV_R1_PEOPLE, CT_COV_R1_COVALT, CT_COV_R1_RAVENS, CT_COV_R1_CLOCKWORK, CT_COV_R1_PERPETUUM, CT_COV_R1_DIFFERENCEENGINE,  CT_COV_R1_ARMY, CT_COV_R1_NOTE.

[These topics may only be fired once.]
Rule for firing a fired conversation topic that is clustered with CT_COV_R1_MYSELF:
	say "I've already talked to him about that." instead;

After firing CT_COV_R1_ARMY:
	change the second-state of Covalt to 2;

