CT_COV_R2_MYSELF is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Then the [as a noun]Figure[end as] found me and knocked me out,' I tell him, finishing my story.". The response text is "'Yes, yes.' He’s not listening – brows bent, deep in thought.". 
CT_COV_R2_BALLOON is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'I’m sorry about your [as a noun]skylight[end as].'". The response text is "'Never mind my [as a noun]skylight[end as],' he answers, crossly. 'I don’t want no sorries from half-dead children!'".
CT_COV_R2_CHURCH is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Do you think the [as a noun]Figure[end as]’ll go back to the Cathedral?' I ask.". The response text is "'The [as a noun]Figure[end as]? Certainly,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] says. 'We know what he’s wanting, after all, don’t we? And I don’t suppose getting fingers round your throat will have changed that for him.'".
CT_COV_R2_CLERGY is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'We should warn someone in the Church.'". The response text is "'You have any proof?' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] replies angrily. 'You’ve given yourself a rusty enough name already today.' Then suddenly he’s grinning. 'They don’t listen to rats like us, rat.'".
CT_COV_R2_PEOPLE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "He won’t know them.".
CT_COV_R2_COVALT is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'What are you thinking?' I ask.". The response text is "'Can’t you guess?' he replies.".
CT_COV_R2_RAVENS is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Are your [as a noun]birds[end as] all right?'". The response text is "He waves the question away unanswered.".
CT_COV_R2_DIFFERENCEENGINE is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'Surely the [as a noun]Difference Engine[end as] could tell us what’s going on…'". The response text is "He laughs bitterly. 'We don’t need an [as a noun]Engine[end as] for that no more. Got a perfectly good rig of springs up here.' He taps his temple.".
CT_COV_R2_ARMY is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'The clockwork men…'". The response text is "'All had [as a noun]hatches[end as] in their guts, I heard you. You see the cogs on this don’t you?'".
CT_COV_R2_PERPETUUM is a conversation topic. The enquiry text is "'The [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as],' I say. 'The [as a noun]Figure[end as] wants it for the army?'". The response text is "'He’s going to make a copy,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] says heavily. 'Give each one a heart that never needs no winding. Imagine [as a noun]soldiers[end as] that can't never be stopped. More like a plague than an [as a noun]army[end as].'[paragraph break]'But for what?'[paragraph break][as a noun]Covalt[end as] shrugs. 'We won’t find out. Copying the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as]? That’s like jamming a second spring into a working balance. Too much power. Or too much of something.' In a moment [as a noun]Covalt[end as] is on his feet again. 'Here’s how I see it. We need to stop the [as a noun]Figure[end as] but we can’t. We stop him today and he’ll be back tomorrow. He’s going to steal that [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] and he won't never give up, so somehow we’ve got to put the chocks in <Italic>after</Italic> that.'[paragraph break]I'm shaking my head. Doesn't make any sense.[paragraph break]He shakes his head too. 'I’ll be widder-wound if I can see how. But that's how it stands.'".

CT_COV_R2_MYSELF is clustered with CT_COV_R2_BALLOON, CT_COV_R2_CHURCH, CT_COV_R2_CLERGY, CT_COV_R2_PEOPLE, CT_COV_R2_COVALT, CT_COV_R2_RAVENS, CT_COV_R2_PERPETUUM, CT_COV_R2_DIFFERENCEENGINE,  CT_COV_R2_ARMY, CT_COV_R2_NOTE.

[These topics may only be fired once.]
Rule for firing a fired conversation topic that is clustered with CT_COV_R2_MYSELF:
	say "I've already talked to him about that." instead;

CT_COV_R2_NOTE is a conversation topic. 
Rule for firing CT_COV_R2_NOTE:
	fire CT_COV_R1_NOTE.

Rule for firing CT_COV_R2_BALLOON:
	fire CT_COV_R1_BALLOON;

[If we ask Covalt about himself a second time, it is the same as asking about the Perpetuum - but without the usual enquiry text.]

First for firing fired CT_COV_R2_COVALT:
	if the enquiry text of CT_COV_R2_COVALT is not "":
		say the enquiry text of CT_COV_R2_COVALT;
	change the enquiry text of CT_COV_R2_PERPETUUM to "";
	fire CT_COV_R2_PERPETUUM;

[If we respond cluelessly to either of Covalt's prompts, it is the same as asking him about himself for the second time -- only without even that enquiry text!]

First after firing unfired CT_COV_R2_COVALT:
	ask DQ_COV_R2_GUESS;

First after firing unfired CT_COV_R2_ARMY:
	ask DQ_COV_R2_GUESS;

DQ_COV_R2_GUESS is a direct question.

A negative response rule for DQ_COV_R2_GUESS:
	now CT_COV_R2_COVALT is fired; [as though it were a repeat firing]
	change the enquiry text of CT_COV_R2_COVALT to "";
	fire CT_COV_R2_COVALT; [thereby firing the Perpetuum response only]

A affirmative response rule for DQ_COV_R2_GUESS:
	now CT_COV_R2_COVALT is fired; [as though it were a repeat firing]
	change the enquiry text of CT_COV_R2_COVALT to "";
	fire CT_COV_R2_COVALT; [thereby firing the Perpetuum response only]

[Finally, the above mechanisms funnel conversation through to the Perpetuum quip]

After firing CT_COV_R2_PERPETUUM:
	change the second-state of Covalt to 3;

