Chapter 3 - Please Insert Coin

Section 1 - Items available



Medicine is a kind of thing.

Some oil of vitriol is a medicine. The description is "A small glass [as a noun]vial[end as] filled with an emerald green [as a noun]oil[end as]."
Understand "small", "glass", "vial", "filled", "with", "emerald", "green", "oil", "liquid", "liquids" as the oil of vitriol.

The Tincture of Morphos is a medicine, proper-named. The description is "A glass [as a noun]bottle[end as] filled with a clear [as a noun]liquid[end as] that sparkles like crystal.".
Understand "small", "glass", "bottle", "filled", "with", "clear", "sparkling/sparkly", "crystal", "liquid", "liquids" as the Tincture of Morphos.

Some poppy seed-pods are a medicine. The description is "A handful of tiny [as a noun]poppy seed-pods[end as]."
Understand "handful", "tiny", "seed", "seeds", "pod", "pods", "herb", "herbs" as the poppy seed-pods.

Rule for printing the name of the oil of vitriol when we are inserting silver coins into a tiny door:
	say "little vial of green oil";	

Rule for printing the name of the Tincture of Morphos when we are inserting silver coins into a tiny door:
	say "small bottle of some clear, evil-looking liquid";

Rule for printing the name of the poppy seed-pods when we are inserting silver coins into a tiny door:
	say "few dark green seed pods";

Instead of eating or drinking medicine:
	say "No chance. I’m not experimenting on myself!";

Section 2 - Inner Workings

Instead of buying a tiny door when the player has silver coins:
	try inserting the silver coins into the noun;

Instead of taking a tiny door when the player has silver coins:
	try inserting the silver coins into the noun.

Before removing a tiny door from the tiny-doors: [ this catches "take foxglove from machine" ]
	try buying the noun instead. 

Instead of buying or taking a tiny door:
	say "I've no money left."

Instead of inserting the silver coins into a tiny door:
	abide by the vending machine rules for the second noun;

The vending machine rules are an object-based rulebook.
The vending machine rulebook has an object called the vended item.

First vending machine rule for door A4:
	change the vended item to the oil of vitriol;

First vending machine rule for door B2:
	change the vended item to the poppy seed-pods;

First vending machine rule for door C2:
	change the vended item to the tincture of morphos;

A vending machine rule when the sleeping drug is on-stage:
	say "I've got my [as a noun]sleeping drug[end as] - that's all I came here for, now it's time to leave!" instead.

A vending machine rule when the vended item is not nothing:
	if the vended item is on-stage:
		say "I’ve already got that ingredient from the drawer." instead;

First vending machine rule for door D1 when TRIG_DOOR_D1 is unfired:
	fire TRIG_DOOR_D1 instead;

TRIG_DOOR_D1 is a trigger.
For firing TRIG_DOOR_D1: say "The price on that door is a colossal 16 minutes!";

[Had to change name of "effect" column in table because it interferes with the "Menus" extension. --JM]

[Last vending machine rule for a tiny door (called x) when the vended item is nothing:
	if the parts-list is unexamined:
		say "Guessing would be a bad idea - I'd better look at what's on offer first." instead;
	choose row with a tiny door of x in the table of autopothecary vending machine slots;  
	say "[one of]I don’t know. I’ve only got [count of silver coins in words] coin[s] and I wouldn’t want to buy the wrong thing.[or]But that's [product entry], [effect entry]! What good would that be?[or]Buy [product entry], [effect entry]? I don't think that'll help me catch the Figure![or]No amount of [product entry] is going send the Figure to sleep![or]I don't think [product entry] is the right thing to buy.[in random order]" instead;]

Last vending machine rule for a tiny door (called x) when the vended item is nothing:
	if the parts-list is unexamined:
		say "Guessing would be a bad idea - I'd better look at what's on offer first." instead;
	choose row with a tiny door of x in the table of autopothecary vending machine slots;  
	say "[one of]I don’t know. I’ve only got [count of silver coins in words] [as a noun]coin[s][end as] and I wouldn’t want to buy the wrong thing.[or]But that's [product entry], [purpose entry]! What good would that be?[or]Buy [product entry], [purpose entry]? I don't think that'll help me catch the [as a noun]Figure[end as]![or]No amount of [product entry] is going send the [as a noun]Figure[end as] to sleep![or]I don't think [product entry] is the right thing to buy.[in random order]" instead;


Last vending machine rule for a tiny door (called x) when the vended item is not nothing and the count of silver coins is 1 and the player is not honest:
	if TRIG_LAST_COIN is unfired:
		change the remembered slot of DQ_COIN to x;
		fire TRIG_LAST_COIN instead;
	otherwise:
		now the player is honest;
		say "You chicken, Wren. [run paragraph on]";

Last vending machine rule for a tiny door (called x) when the vended item is not nothing:
	decrement the count of the silver coins by 1;
	if the count of the silver coins is at most 0:
		remove the silver coins from play;
	now the player carries the vended item;
	say "[one of]The [as a noun]coin[end as] disappears into the [as a noun]slot[end as] and watching it go is a bit like losing a finger or waking up in the morning when it’s wet and cold and it’s washing day. Then there’s a loud clatter from inside the [as a noun]autopothecary[end as] and the little [as a noun]door[end as] drops open – just long enough for me to snatch out a [vended item].[or]I drop in the second [as a noun]coin[end as] and this time I’m ready for the [as a noun]door[end as], managing to get out a [vended item] without trapping my fingers on the way out.[or]The last [as a noun]coin[end as] disappears, gone for good into this stupid little machine. In return all I get is a [vended item].[stopping]";

Section 3 - A Moral Dilemma

Yourself can be honest, dishonest, or morally neutral. Yourself is morally neutral.

TRIG_LAST_COIN is a trigger.

Rule for firing unfired TRIG_LAST_COIN:
	say "The [as a noun]last coin[end as]... couldn’t I make do with the ingredients we've got?";
	ask DQ_COIN;

DQ_COIN is a direct question. DQ_COIN has a tiny door called the remembered slot.

An affirmative response rule for DQ_COIN:
	now the player is dishonest;
	say "I’m sure what we’ve got will be strong enough. I slip the [as a noun]last coin[end as] somewhere safe where [as a noun]Covalt[end as] won't see it. Time, then, to prepare the other [as a noun]ingredients[end as], in the [as a noun]press[end as].";

A negative response rule for DQ_COIN:
	now the player is honest;
	try inserting the silver coins into the remembered slot of DQ_COIN;


Every turn when TRIG_LAST_COIN has been fired for exactly one turn and the player is morally neutral:
	now the player is dishonest;
	say "I’m sure what we’ve got will be strong enough. I slip the [as a noun]last coin[end as] somewhere safe where [as a noun]Covalt[end as] won't see it. Time to finish up making this drug.";
	

Chapter 4 - Drug Press

Section 1 - Description

The autopothecary press is a container, scenery, in the Autopothecary Booth. "The [as a noun]press[end as] is a small contraption for mixing drugs together. [one of]Since it’s meant to be used in the middle of the night by people with roaring headaches and upset bellies it’s got [as a noun]instructions[end as] all over it and it couldn’t be easier. [once only]Right now, the little [as a noun]tin disc[end as] above the machine is displaying: '[press status message]'".

The reading matter of the autopothecary press is "The little [as a noun]tin disc[end as] above the machine displays '[press status message]'[paragraph break]";

Understand "neat", "little", "lever", "tin", "disc" as the autopothecary press.

The autopothecary press has a number called the state. The state of the autopothecary press is 1.

To say press status message:
	if the state of the autopothecary press is:
		-- 1: say "Add Herbs and lift [as a noun]lever[end as].[run paragraph on]";
		-- 2: say "Add Herbs and lift [as a noun]lever[end as].[run paragraph on]";
		-- 3: say "Add liquids.[run paragraph on]";
		-- 4: say "Lift [as a noun]lever[end as] if ready to combine all ingredients.[run paragraph on]";
		-- 5: say "Lift [as a noun]lever[end as] if ready to combine all ingredients.[run paragraph on]";
		-- 6: say "Add Herbs and lift [as a noun]lever[end as].[run paragraph on]";

Section 2 - Drug Adding

The drug-adding rules are an object-based rulebook.

Does the player mean inserting a medicine into the autopothecary press: it is likely.

Instead of inserting something into the autopothecary press:
	abide by the drug-adding rules for the noun;

A drug-adding rule for a thing (called x) when x is not medicine:
	say "I don't want to break it." instead;

A drug-adding rule for the poppy seed-pods:
	say "Following the [as a noun]instructions[end as] on the sign, I brush the poppy seeds off my palm and into the press.";
	remove the poppy seed-pods from play;
	change the state of the autopothecary press to 2;
	rule succeeds;

A drug-adding rule for the oil of vitriol when the state of the autopothecary press is less than 3:
	say "The little sign says 'Add herbs and raise [as a noun]lever[end as],' but the [as a noun]oil[end as] isn’t a herb." instead;

A drug-adding rule for the tincture of Morphos when the state of the autopothecary press is less than 3:
	say "The little sign says 'Add herbs and raise [as a noun]lever[end as],' but the [as a noun]tincture[end as] isn’t a herb." instead;

A drug-adding rule for the oil of vitriol:
	say "I drip the contents of the [as a noun]vial[end as] into the funnel[if the state of the autopothecary press is 3]. The [as a noun]tin sign[end as] rotates to read 'lift [as a noun]lever[end as] if ready.'[otherwise].[end if]";
	remove the oil of vitriol from play;
	increment the state of the autopothecary press by 1;
	rule succeeds;

A drug-adding rule for the tincture of morphos:
	say "The [as a noun]Morphos[end as] falls in tiny starlight splashes into the bowl of the [as a noun]press[end as]. There’s a faint bitter smell that makes my head spin... [if the state of the autopothecary press is 3]The [as a noun]tin sign[end as] rotates to read 'lift [as a noun]lever[end as] if ready.' [end if][paragraph break]";
	remove the tincture of morphos from play;
	increment the state of the autopothecary press by 1;
	rule succeeds;

Section 3 - Drug Pressing

Instead of pushing or taking or switching on the autopothecary press:
	try pulling the autopothecary press instead;

Instead of pulling the autopothecary press:
	abide by the drug-pressing rules;

The drug-pressing rules are a rulebook.

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 1:
	say "I give the [as a noun]lever[end as] a twitch. The two plates inside come neatly together, then separate out again since there’s nothing inside to squeeze";
	if the player is dishonest and the poppy seed-pods have not been on-stage:
		[ then we let the player continue on, regardless ] 
		change the state of the autopothecary press to 3;
		say ". The [as a noun]disc[end as] on the front of the machine rotates to read 'Now add liquids.'" instead;
	say "." instead.

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 2:
	change the state of the autopothecary press to 3;
	say "I push the [as a noun]lever[end as] up. Two plates inside the machine come together to squeeze the [as a noun]pods[end as], releasing golden oil into a bowl below. The [as a noun]disc[end as] on the front of the machine rotates to read 'Now add liquids.'" instead;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 3:
	say "I push the [as a noun]lever[end as] again, giving the [as a noun]seed pods[end as] another squash, but there’s no more oil to drain out." instead;

TRIG_LAST_MINUTE is a trigger.

Rule for firing unfired TRIG_LAST_MINUTE:
	say "I’ve still got [as a noun]one minute[end as] left to spend. If there’s something else that’ll make this drug more powerful I’d better find it." instead;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 4 and the count of the silver coins is 0:
	say "I’ve still got my third ingredient left to put in." instead;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 4:
	if the player is dishonest:
		change the state of the autopothecary press to 5;
		anonymously abide by the drug-production rule;
		[stop]
	if TRIG_LAST_MINUTE is unfired:
		fire TRIG_LAST_MINUTE instead;
	now the player is dishonest;
	say "I’ll keep the [as a noun]third coin[end as], then. For myself.";
	change the state of the autopothecary press to 5;
	anonymously abide by the drug-production rule;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 5:
	assert that the player is not dishonest issuing "Player is not dishonest.";
	now the sleeping drug is strong;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 5 (this is the drug-production rule):
	now the player carries the sleeping drug;
	now the state of the autopothecary press is 6;
	say "The [as a noun]lever[end as] springs up then down, clamping a lid onto the bowl inside the machine. There’s a brief moment of spinning and then the whole [as a noun]press[end as] tips over and out drains a [as a noun]murky liquid[end as] to be caught in a [as a noun]bottle[end as] below. That’s my [as a noun]sleeping drug[end as]! Gingerly, I pick it up." instead;

A drug-pressing rule when the state of the autopothecary press is 6:
	say "The machine is empty." instead;

Every turn when the player is in the Autopothecary Booth and the sleeping drug has been handled for exactly one turns:
	say "The machine flips back over and rights itself, ready for the next customer."

Section 4 - A Sleeping Drug

The sleeping drug is medicine. The description is "A [as a noun]little bottle[end as] of a [as a noun]murky grey coloured liquid[end as]. Perfect for the [as a noun]Figure[end as][if weak].  I only hope it’s strong enough[end if]." 

Understand "little", "bottle", "bottle of" as the sleeping drug.
Understand "murky", "grey", "gray", "coloured/colored", "liquid" as the sleeping drug.


The sleeping drug can be weak or strong. The sleeping drug is weak.

Instead of dropping or attacking the sleeping drug:
	say "This thing is precious, I can't lose it!"

Last Before inserting the sleeping drug into something:
	try dropping the sleeping drug instead.
Last Before putting the sleeping drug on something:
	try dropping the sleeping drug instead.

Before putting the sleeping drug on the workbench:
	try giving the sleeping drug to Covalt instead.

Instead of giving the sleeping drug to Covalt:
	remove the sleeping drug from play;
	say "[as a noun]Covalt[end as] barely looks up from his work. 'I’m sure it’ll do,' he snaps. 'Stick it over there and don’t say anything else at any point until I’ve got all this work done.' On the bench in front of him is half a box and it doesn’t look bad – the little ball rolling down the zigzag track, the casements either side that flip-flop the surface. And on the inside is a tight spring attached to a little hammer from a bell-strike ready to the break the glass, right about a small needle.[paragraph break]Gingerly [as a noun]Covalt[end as] picks up the [as a noun]bottle[end as], and fits it into the box. 'Don’t press the casements,' he warns. 'Or you’ll fire the needle. Don’t forget that.' With slow delicacy he clicks a panel into place.[paragraph break]'I could go to the gallows for making this,' [as a noun]Covalt[end as] says. 'They won’t thank me. They won’t thank either of us. They’ll be grateful and then they’ll send us up the scaffold. But we’ll face that when the hands come round for it. You ready?'[paragraph break]I nod. What else can I do?[paragraph break]'Sneak into the vaults and swap this over. So good luck, and I’m not coming with you. If they ask you where you got this from you say it fell from the stars.' And then he chucks me out and slams the door.[paragraph break]And then I’m off, on my own again, back on my way to the [as a noun]Cathedral[end as] of Time.";
	now the player carries the decoy Perpetuum;
	end the chapter;
	say "Like the lowliest ratchet in the bottom of a gear-train, I move in darkness. Through the streets of the [as a noun]city[end as], sticking close to the walls. Carrying the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] – or something that looks so much like it that I can’t afford to be seen. My only hope would be that they mistook me for a scruffy little angel.[paragraph break]Lucky it’s easy to find my way. The [as a noun]Cathedral[end as]’s great dome looms over all of [as a noun]St Phillip[end as], blotting out stars. I head deeper into darkness until it fills the entire northeastern sky, and that’s when I’m beside the great [as a noun]Western door[end as].";
	move the player to the Public Yard;

Book 10 - Return to the Cathedral

When Return to the Cathedral begins:
	now the West Door [public entrance to the Cathedral] is unlocked;
	now the West Door is open;
	remove the glimpsed monks from play;
	remove the glimpsed Perpetuum from play;
	remove the Chanting Monks from play;
	move the great-engine to the Cathedral Choir;
	remove the secret construction ladder from play;
	move the real Perpetuum Mobile to the Steel Altar; [in the Inner Vault]

The decoy Perpetuum Mobile is a thing. The description is "[as a noun]Covalt[end as]'s done an incredible job. I only caught a glimpse of the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] before, but this is exactly like it. The [as a noun]board[end as] on top, with the [as a noun]track[end as] for the [as a noun]ball-bearing[end as], and a few tiny [as a noun]lever[end as]s sticking from the sides like ant's legs. And everything else (and in this case, <Italic>nothing</Italic> else) hidden away inside."

Understand "dummy", "tiny levers/lever", "levers", "bearing", "case", "dark wood", "wood", "tilting", "board", "ball-bearing", "groove", "grooved", "path", "track", "gold", "brass", "ball", "ball bearing", "mechanism", "fake", "false" as the decoy perpetuum mobile.

Instead of dropping the decoy Perpetuum when TRIG_SECRET_PANEL is unfired:
	say "I need it. I can’t afford to lose it in the dark.";

Instead of dropping the decoy Perpetuum when TRIG_SECRET_PANEL is fired and the location is not the Cathedral Choir:
	say "I want to keep it as near me as I can.";

After dropping the decoy Perpetuum:
	now the decoy Perpetuum is scenery;
	say "I tuck the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] into the shadows by the [as a noun]stalls[end as]. Barely visible to anyone – I hope." instead;

Part 1 - Public Yard

Return to the Cathedral is a scene. Return To The Cathedral begins when Return to Covalt's ends. Return To The Cathedral ends when TRIG_FIGURE_NOT_HURT is fired.

Instead of making to leave when in the Public Yard: try going east.
Instead of going inside when in the Public Yard: try going east.

The Public Yard is a room. "The public square where the people come to hear the edicts and songs and gather before Mass, Volume and Compline. It’s empty now except for a towering statue of [as a noun]St Newton[end as], gazing thoughtfully up at the stars. The [as a noun]great door[end as] of the [as a noun]Cathedral[end as] is open to the east.[one of][paragraph break]There’s no time to lose.[once only]"

The silhouetted Cathedral of Time is scenery, in the Public Yard. "The [as a noun]Cathedral[end as] raises spires like pins in a pin-cushion, only just visible as gaps in the stars. The glowing face of the rose window clock puts the time as a quarter to midnight. The [as a noun]door[end as] to the [as a noun]Cathedral[end as] is open.". The printed name of the silhouetted Cathedral is "Cathedral". Understand "church" as the silhouetted Cathedral of Time.

The statue of St Isaac Newton is scenery, in the Public Yard. "[as a noun]Newton[end as] stands, [as a noun]apple[end as] in one hand, [as a noun]skull[end as] in the other. If he let go of either one I’d be crushed like a beetle in Drake’s bunkroom.". The printed name of the statue of St Isaac Newton is "statue of St Newton".

Instead of searching the statue of St Isaac Newton:
	say "He carries an [as a noun]apple[end as] and a [as a noun]skull[end as]."

Instead of climbing the statue of St Isaac Newton:
	say "It's tall enough to be quite a climb - but I've done enough climbing today (hopefully).";

Instead of pushing or pulling or turning St Isaac Newton:
	say "He's enormous. I can't go pushing him around (and he's a Saint, so I shouldn't, either.)";

Understand "apple", "skull" as the statue of St Isaac Newton.

Rule for printing the description of the West Door when in the Public Yard during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The [as a noun]great door[end as] is open, just enough to let someone slip inside. Probably left that way for the [as a noun]Figure[end as]. I need to be quick.";

Instead of approaching the West Door: 
	try going east.

After going through the West Door from the Public Yard during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "I slip [one of][or]back [stopping]inside.";
	continue the action;

Instead of closing the open West Door during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "It’s too heavy for me to move.";

Instead of entering or approaching the silhouetted Cathedral of Time:
	try going east;

Part 2 - Cathedral Entrance

Rule for printing the description of the Cathedral Entrance during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The [as a noun]Cathedral[end as] to the north is almost pitch dark, with a few [as a noun]false stars[end as] – [as a noun]candles[end as], reflecting off the [as a noun]polished brass[end as] and the [as a noun]windows[end as]. The huge [as a noun]doors[end as] east and south are sealed fast: the door west should have been but it’s been left open[one of]. [paragraph break]I need to get down to the Crypt, to plant the [as a noun]decoy[end as]. And fast – before the [as a noun]Figure[end as] beats me to it.[or].[stopping]";

Rule for printing the description of the entry seal during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The seal is just a circle in the half-light.";

Instead of doing something when the Great Doors are physically involved during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The [as a noun]doors[end as] are shut fast.";

Instead of doing something when the East Door is physically involved during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The [as a noun]doors[end as] are shut fast.";

Rule for printing the description of the West Door when in the Cathedral Entrance during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The small [as a noun]west door[end as] is a crack ajar.";

Instead of closing the open West Door when in the Cathedral Entrance during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "It’s too heavy for me to shift. I can’t keep the [as a noun]Figure[end as] out.";

Instead of going through the West Door from the Cathedral Entrance during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "No time for turning back!";

Instead of making to leave when in the Cathedral Entrance during Return to the Cathedral:
	try going west.

Instead of going from the Cathedral Entrance to the Public Yard during Return to the Cathedral:
	say "The east door is now closed. I can't get back to the [as a noun]Abbey[end as]."



Section 1 - Stars and Candles

Some false-stars are privately-named, scenery, in the Cathedral Entrance. Understand "candle", "light", "lights", "candles", "star",  "polished brass", "brass", "windows", "false stars", "stars" as the false-stars when Return to the Cathedral is happening. "They gleam from the depths of the dark Cathedral." The printed name is "candle lights".

Instead of approaching the false-stars: try going north.

Instead of doing something when the false-stars are physically involved:
	say "I creep into the [as a noun]Cathedral[end as].";
	try going north.

Part 3 - Lower Nave

Rule for printing the description of the Lower Nave during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "Oak [as a noun]pews[end as] are sleeping either side of the aisle. I can barely see the shrines either side: a little [as a noun]orange light[end as] leaks in from the east. Past the second [as a noun]seal[end as] to the north, the nave continues.";

Rule for printing the description of the lower seal during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "The [as a noun]seal[end as] is just a circle in the half-light.";

Instead of going south from the Lower Nave during Return To The Cathedral:
