	continue the action;

An orange-light is a privately-named, scenery thing. Understand "orange", "light", "little" as the orange-light. "The [as a noun]light[end as] comes from the Shrine of the Saints, ever so faintly."  The printed name is "orange light".

Instead of doing something when the orange-light is physically involved:
	say "It's just [as a noun]light[end as], and thin [as a noun]light[end as] too."

Before approaching or entering the orange-light:
	try going east instead.

Chapter 2 - Pews

Rule for printing the description of a pew during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "Rows of varnished oak [as a noun]pews[end as].";

Instead of entering or hiding inside or hiding under or hiding behind a pew when Calvin's Patrol has not happened during Return To The Cathedral:
	say "Now is not a time to pray, or hide!";

Before searching, reading or opening a hymnal during Return to the Cathedral:
	say "It is too dark to read." instead.

Instead of hiding from view during Calvin's Patrol:
	if the player can see a pew (called the hiding place):
		try entering the hiding place instead;
	say "I can't see anywhere to hide!"

Instead of entering or standing on or sitting on or hiding inside or hiding under or hiding behind a pew (called the hiding place) during Calvin's Patrol:
	say "[one of]I dive in between the [as a noun]pews[end as][or]I shuffle in between the [as a noun]pews[end as][or]I drop to my knees between the [as a noun]pews[end as][at random][if the player carries a lit candle], and blow out my [as a noun]candle[end as][end if].";
	move the player to the hiding place, without printing a room description;
	while the player carries a lit candle:
