	try dropping the noun;
	
Last Instead of putting something on the steel altar:
  say "I mustn't leave any clues for the [as a noun]Figure[end as]. If this trap is going to work it must be perfect - like clockwork!"

Instead of dropping the real Perpetuum Mobile:
	say "I didn't come all this way to leave it behind!"

Section 3 - Arrival of the Figure


[ NOT SURE what this was meant to do? But it prints blank responses!!

Rule for implicitly opening the iron vault door when in the Inner Vault:
	do nothing;
]

Instead of opening the iron vault door when in the Inner Vault and the real perpetuum mobile is on the steel altar:
	say "I can't go yet!";

Instead of opening the iron vault door when in the Inner Vault and the decoy perpetuum mobile is on the steel altar and TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL is unfired:
	fire TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL;

Instead of opening the iron vault door when in the Inner Vault:
	say "The [as a noun]Figure[end as] is right outside! I'll never slip past him, it's impossible! I'm <Italic>trapped</Italic>!";

Instead of listening when TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL is fired and TRIG_FIGURE_ENTERS is not fired:
	say "I can hear him, outside the door, his low voice murmuring to the Brass [as a noun]Head[end as].";

TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL is a trigger.

At the time when the figure comes:
	fire TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL;

Rule for firing unfired TRIG_FIGURE_ARRIVAL:
	the figure enters in two turns from now;
	say "That's when I hear it. The voice of the Brass [as a noun]Head[end as].[paragraph break]'Time. Is.'[paragraph break]It must be the [as a noun]Figure[end as]. Outside the [as a noun]door[end as].";

TRIG_FIGURE_ENTERS is a trigger.

At the time when the figure enters:
	fire TRIG_FIGURE_ENTERS;

Rule for firing unfired TRIG_FIGURE_ENTERS:
	say "The [as a noun]door[end as] opens[unless we are hiding behind the iron vault door] and I press myself quickly behind it[end if]. Darkness enters like cold night wind through a hole in the roof. It is the [as a noun]Figure[end as], moving as fast as only he can.[paragraph break]He wastes no time and goes straight to the [as a noun]altar[end as]. It’s all I can do to keep quiet while I’m watching. He picks it up – for a moment I think the trap has failed, but then I understand that [as a noun]Covalt[end as] has built it better than that: delaying the sting to make certain of getting the victim.[paragraph break]There’s a <Italic>crack</Italic> as the needle springs out. The [as a noun]Figure[end as] stops still. That’s it, I’m thinking, I’ve got him. I’ve got him!";

TRIG_FIGURE_NOT_HURT is a trigger;

After reading a command when TRIG_FIGURE_ENTERS is fired and TRIG_FIGURE_NOT_HURT is unfired:
	fire TRIG_FIGURE_NOT_HURT;
	consider the scene changing rules;
	reject the player's command;

Rule for firing unfired TRIG_FIGURE_NOT_HURT:
	say "I'm frozen to the spot as, slowly, the [as a noun]Figure[end as] puts down the [as a noun]decoy[end as]. He pulls the needle curiously from his arm. From the tilt of his hood I can see he’s regarding it – firstly curiously, then with anger.[paragraph break]He is completely unaffected[if the player is dishonest]. Maybe I should have made the potion properly, like [as a noun]Covalt[end as] told me to! Or maybe it wouldn't have mattered. Maybe[else]. It seems[end if] the [as a noun]Figure[end as] can run and jump and climb, and can't be hurt at all. He's perfect.[paragraph break]In a single movement like a cat with a rabbit he tears the [as a noun]decoy[end as] apart. Guts and gears spill everywhere. The [as a noun]Figure[end as] picks one up, turns it over – then dashes away.[paragraph break]At least I’ve scared him, I think. But of course, I haven’t. [as a noun]Covalt[end as] made the [as a noun]decoy[end as] well, but he made it in a hurry, using whatever parts he could find. Parts that still bear his stamp. And his name.[paragraph break]A moment later, I’ve got the [as a noun]Perpetuum[end as] under one arm and I’m racing out the door.";

