Book U - User Interface for Windows 8

Part 0 - Workarounds for 5Z71 Eccentricities

A direction has a text called the printed name.
The printed name of up is "up".
The printed name of down is "down".
The printed name of inside is "inside".
The printed name of outside is "outside".
The printed name of north is "north".
The printed name of south is "south".
The printed name of east is "east".
The printed name of west is "west".
The printed name of northeast is "northeast".
The printed name of northwest is "northwest".
The printed name of southeast is "southeast".
The printed name of southwest is "southwest".

[EU: ``when the location encloses ...'' doesn't compile to an object tree traversal in 5Z71, which makes it *very* slow.  We use this routine and phrase to force object tree traversals.]
Include (-
	[ textfyre_tree_next object ancestor;
		if (child(object)) {
			return child(object);
		}
		while (~~sibling(object)) {
			object = parent(object);
			if (object == ancestor) {
				return nothing;
			}
		}
		return sibling(object);
	];
-).
To repeat with (I - a nonexisting object variable) running through (A - an object) begin -- end: (-
	for ({I} = {A}: {I} = textfyre_tree_next({I}, {A}):)
-).

Part 1 - Infrastructure for Word Suggestion

Chapter - Parsable Name

Every thing has a text called the parsable name.

To decide what text is the suggestion for (O - an object):
	if O is a thing and the parsable name of O is not empty:
		decide on the parsable name of O;
	decide on the printed name of O.

Chapter - Word Categories

A word category is a kind of value.  The word categories are verb, substantive [because "noun" already has a meaning in Inform], compass point [because "direction" already has a meaning in Inform], adverb, adjective, article, preposition, conjunction, and answer.

A word category has a list of texts called the vocabulary.
A word category can be suggested or unsuggested.

To say the plural of (C - a word category):
	say "[C]s".

Chapter - Suggestions

[EU: Unfortunately, 5Z71 doesn't have hash tables.]

[Suggested-as relates various texts to various word categories.
The verb to be suggested as implies the suggested-as relation.

To suggest (T - some text) as (C - a word category):
	now T is suggested as C.
To suggest (O - an object) as (C - a word category):
	now the suggestion for O is suggested as C.
To unsuggest (T - some text) as (C - a word category):
	now T is not suggested as C.
To unsuggest anything suggested as (C - a word category):
	now no text is suggested as C.]

[EU: So we do this instead.  If performance is a problem, we'll drop to I6 and get fancier.]

A word category has a list of texts called the suggestions.
Suggested-as relates a texts (called the suggestion) to a word categories (called the suggestion category) when the suggestion is listed in the suggestions of the suggestion category.
The verb to be suggested as implies the suggested-as relation.

To suggest (T - some text) as (C - a word category):
	add T to the suggestions of C, if absent.
To suggest (O - an object) as (C - a word category):
	add the suggestion for O to the suggestions of C, if absent.
To unsuggest (T - some text) as (C - a word category):
	remove T from the suggestions of C.
To unsuggest anything suggested as (C - a word category):
	truncate the suggestions of C to zero entries.

[EU: Further, we need this workaround for a 5Z71 bug.]

To decide what list of texts is texts suggested as (C - a word category):
	decide on the suggestions of C.

Chapter - Presenting Suggestions

Presenting suggestions is an activity.

Presenting a suggestion is an activity.
The presenting a suggestion activity has a word category called the category to present; the presenting a suggestion activity has a text called the word to present.

[EU: 5Z71 doesn't give us access to activity variables outside of activity rules, so we relay them via a first before rule.]
The global variable for communicating the category to present is a word category that varies; the global variable for communicating the word to present is some text that varies.
First before presenting a suggestion (this is the communicate category and word to present rule):
	now the category to present is the global variable for communicating the category to present;
	now the word to present is the global variable for communicating the word to present.

To present (T - some text) as (C - a word category):
	[EU: See just above for the rule that gets these values into the activity under 5Z71.]
	now global variable for communicating the category to present is C;
	now global variable for communicating the word to present is T;
	begin the presenting a suggestion activity;
	[EU: This is how we would do it if we had full dynamic scoping.]
	[now the category to present is C;
	now the word to present is T;]
	if [we consult the "for" rules, and none of them intervene, so that this code must be responsible itself for] handling the presenting a suggestion activity:
		do nothing[, because we're probably running in an environment where suggestions aren't supported];
	end the presenting a suggestion activity.

For presenting suggestions (this is the standard presenting suggestions rule):
	repeat with the category running through word categories:
		repeat with the candidate word running through the vocabulary of the category:
			if the candidate word is suggested as the category:
				present the candidate word as the category;
				unsuggest the candidate word as the category;
		[EU: 5Z71 uses return by copy (a policy that survived up through 6G60), we can't access the suggestions by phrase without a serious slowdown.  Hence the unfortunate use of direct access on the next line.]
		repeat with the candidate word running through [texts suggested as] the suggestions of [end performance tweak] the category:
			present the candidate word as the category;
		unsuggest anything suggested as the category.

To present suggestions:
	carry out the presenting suggestions activity.

Chapter - Presenting Suggestions in Glk

Before presenting suggestions when FyreVM is not present:
	now every word category is unsuggested;
	say "Suggestions:[run paragraph on]".

For presenting a suggestion when FyreVM is not present:
	if the category to present is unsuggested:
		say "[line break][the plural of the category to present]: ";
		now the category to present is suggested;
	otherwise:
		say ", ";
	say "[the word to present][run paragraph on]".

After presenting suggestions when FyreVM is not present:
	say "[line break]".

Chapter - Presenting Suggestions in FyreVM

Before presenting suggestions when FyreVM is present:
	select the words channel;
	say "<suggestions>".

For presenting a suggestion when FyreVM is present:
	say "<[the category to present]>[the word to present]</[the category to present]>[run paragraph on]".

After presenting suggestions when FyreVM is present:
	say "</suggestions>";
	select the main channel.

Chapter - Making Suggestions

The suggesting words rules are a rulebook.

Chapter - Timing Suggestions

[EU: This phrase exists only to make profiling easier.]
To accumulate suggestions:
	follow the suggesting words rules.

Before reading a command:
	accumulate suggestions;
	present suggestions.

Part 2 - Extra Metadata for Suggesting Words in Shadow in the Cathedral

Chapter - Additional Properties

Section - Boilerplate

A thing can be boilerplate.
The backdrop-floor, the backdrop-ceiling, the backdrop-walls, the backdrop-sky, the backdrop-sun, the backdrop-moon, the backdrop-clouds, and the backdrop-sun2 are boilerplate.

Section - False Animates

A thing can be a falsely animate.
The bust of St Isaac Newton and the creatures and the initiates are falsely animate.

Section - Turnables

A thing can be turnable.
The tea-machine key, the refectory clock, a cartesian crank, the crank handle, the elongated chimney [as a noun]pipe[end as], the compass, the large crank, the bolts, the ignition bolt, and the granite column are turnable.

After opening the bird cage when the third-state of Covalt is 1 during Midnight:
	now the Figure Grey is turnable.

Section - Enterable-Suppressing Rooms

A room can be enterable-suppressing.
The Inside Clock Case and the West Clerestory are enterable-suppressing.

Section - Revealed and Unrevealed

A thing can be revealed or unrevealed.  A thing is usually revealed.
A room can be revealed or unrevealed.  A room is usually revealed.

The new gear is unrevealed.
After examining the cabinet of relics:
	now the new gear is revealed.
Before doing something when the noun is the new gear or the second noun is the new gear:
	now the new gear is revealed.

The distant parapet is unrevealed.
After firing SE_MINHAND1:
	now the distant parapet is revealed.

The ornithopter is unrevealed.
After firing TRIG_ROOFTOP_4:
	now the ornithopter is revealed.

The twelve-foot gap is unrevealed.

The glimpse-bedroom is unrevealed.

The glimpse-Clock-Shop is unrevealed.

The glimpse-machine is unrevealed.
After firing CAL_SPOTTED:
	now the glimpse-machine is revealed.
Every turn when the unadmired Difference Engine is visible:
	now the glimpse-machine is revealed.

The leather folder is unrevealed.
Before examining the large oak desk:
	now the leather folder is revealed.
Before searching the large oak desk:
	now the leather folder is revealed.

The office is unrevealed.
When Calculatrix Chase begins:
	now the office is revealed.

The wrench is unrevealed.
Before examining the rubble:
	now the wrench is revealed.
Before taking the wrench:
	now the wrench is revealed.

River 1 and the River 2 are unrevealed.
Before entering the River Thymes:
	now River 1 is revealed;
	now River 2 is revealed.

The ladder-glimpse is unrevealed.

The secret clock door is unrevealed.
When Return To The Cathedral begins:
	now the secret clock door is revealed.

The false-stars are unrevealed.
When Return to the Cathedral begins:
	now the false-stars are revealed.

Section - Chasing Events

A scripted event can be chasing.
CHASE0, CHASE1, CHASE2, CHASE3, and CHASE4 are chasing.

Chapter - Additional Definitions

Section - Distant Scenery

Definition: a thing is distant scenery if it is scenery and it is not in the location.

Section - Takables

Definition: a thing is takeable if it is portable and it is not enclosed by a person.

Section - Readables

Definition: a thing is readable if the reading matter of it is not empty or it is the grey pamphlet or it is a display board or it is the punchcard.

Section - Purported Enterables

Definition: a thing is purportedly enterable if it is enterable or it is a door or it is matched-to locative glimpse backdrop.

Section - Unoccupied Containers

Definition: a thing is unoccupied if it does not enclose the player.

Section - Purportedly Conversationally Available People

Definition: a person is purportedly conversationally available if they are not falsely animate and they are conversationally available.

Section - Misleadingly Singular

Definition:  a thing is misleadingly singular if it is the marble stairs and the location is the Grand Foyer.

Section - Elided-Though-Visible Things

Definition: a thing is elided-though-visible if it is boilerplate or it is unrevealed or it is a locative glimpse backdrop or it is distant scenery or it is misleadingly singular or it is part of something.

