Table of Someone Coming Hints
hint											used
"It wouldn't be a good idea to be found in here."						a number
"But there's no way to get away through the door, or the window."
"You'd better hide somewhere."
"The cot's too small. There's only thing big enough..."
"Remember, Grandfather clocks have large cabinets where the penduluums are..."
"Try hiding inside the clock! And better do it quickly!"

Table of Cannot Hear Hints								
hint											used
"The Abbot is just visible through that keyhole. Maybe you could hear something there?"		a number
"But maybe listening at the keyhole still isn't enough. If there was something you had that could make it louder..."
"There's an old trick to listening at keyholes: using something cup-shaped to amplify the sound..."
"Try putting your glass against the keyhole."

Table of Gone Hints									
hint											used
"Sounds like you need to tell someone what you've heard."					a number
"Get out of the clock and get out of the Abbot's room, before he comes back!"
"The door is to the west - just type WEST to go that way."

Table of What Now Hints
hint											used
"You need to find the Archbishop, in the Cathedral of Time."					a number
"Right now you're in the Abbey of Time, so you'd better leave."
"Once you're in the Hall of the Abbey, you need to keep going southwest until you get out."
"Except there's a spanner in the works, and that's Calvin."
"Either you need to find another way out of the Abbey, or some way of shifting him."
"Time to explore - and you might find Brother Horloge of some interest..."

Table of Drake Hints
hint											used
"Drake is a big pain in your life, Wren. He's the worst there is."					a number
"But luckily, he's boring. Everything he does is clockwork. He likes to stick to a pattern."
"If you can work out which order he walks around the Abbey in, you might be able to dodge him."
"Also, if he's approaching a room where you're standing, you might be able to hide."
"Several of the rooms offer hiding places."
"Try hiding under the Refectory tables - or in the Pantry in the Kitchen!"

Table of Keys Hints
hint											used
"Of course you can't, they're not yours!"							a number
"But you could probably borrow them."
"Except Brother Horloge won't let you. Every time you try and take the keys it's too distracting for him. Perhaps you could distract him in return."
"There seems to be something he wants. Can you figure out what it is?"
"Brother Horloge is a great drinker of tea. Time to brew up a cup!"

Table of Tea Machine Hints
hint											used
"Like all good clockwork machines, the Tea Maker needs a lot of different things to make it go."	a number
"Make sure you EXAMINE it closely. Try pulling the lever to turn it on."
"Some of the things you need are obvious. You can't make tea without tea leaves, or a cup."
"When you've found some tea, put it in the basket. When you've found a cup, put that in the bracket."
"You'll have to fill the kettle up too."
"But what about this missing gear?"
"Have you seen anywhere which might stock replacement gears?"
"Perhaps Brother Reloh can help? (Or, perhaps not)."
"Take one of the new gears from the Cabinet in the Scriptorium. Then put that into the Tea Machine."
"Still stuck? Just pull the lever, and watch it go!"

Table of Owl Hints
hint											used
"If you can't think of anything to do with the owl yet, you must not need it yet."			a number
"If you still can't think of anything to do with the owl, maybe there isn't anything to do with the owl."
"It's Brother Horloge's owl. And it's asleep."

Table of Talk Hints
hint											used
"Most of the monks are very busy. And very crotchety."					a number
"Some of them will talk to you - the Abbot, for instance, if you're brave enough to go back to his quarters."
"Try asking him about something, like clockwork, or the Abbey, or even - gulp! - the Figure in Grey..."

Table of Keys-2 Hints
hint											used
"Have you found anything you could unlock?"						a number
"There are two things the keys will open for you."
"Both are in the same room..."
"Go to the East Refectory."
"You can open the clock and the garden door."

Table of Clock Hints
hint											used
"Once you've got it open, you can reset it."							a number
"...if you're brave enough, but once you start messing with clocks, there's no turning them back!"
"(Well, there is... but metaphorically there isn't. Never mind.)"
"If you're going to reset the clock, you'd better choose a sensible time. A time that will cause Calvin to leave his post, maybe!"
"Perhaps dinner time would be a good choice? Try setting the clock to that."

Table of Garden Hints
hint														used
"That metal hood looks interesting. There might be something underneath it, if you can figure out how the garden works."	a number
"Otherwise, the walls look interesting too. Might be a way out of the Abbey if you can get over them."
"Have you seen anything that might help you get over a wall?"
"This one's up to you - but don't worry, if you can't solve it, you can still get out of the Abbey a different way!"

Table of Archbishop Hints
hint											used
"Well, it's his Cathedral, so he could be anywhere."						a number
"But most likely he'll be in his Library, at the north end above the Choir."
"If you can get through the door..."

Table of Monks Hints
hint											used
"The monks are pretty engrossed in their chanting and prayers."				a number
"In fact, they're so engrossed you can slip right past!"
"You might want to take a look at what's on the altar, however."

Table of Guard Hints
hint															used
"His name is Doric and he works for the Swiss Watch. They can't be bribed and they never fall asleep on the job (or very rarely, anyway)."	a number
"Doric wants two things: written proof, and the Creed of the Church."
"You can also get him out of the way by annoying him."
"Try going to the north end of the Clerestory and throwing something at him."
"Can you make it back round in time to beat him to the door?"
"No? Well, you'd better find that Creed and some written proof then!"

Table of Creed Hints
hint											used
"Maybe you should know the Creed, Wren, but you don't seem to! You'll have to guess."		a number
"Lucky for you, in a world of clockwork people aren't always very imaginative."
"And they like to write everything down."
"Have you noticed the Great Seals on the floor of the Cathedral?"
"You can guess the Creed as many times as you like. If you get close, Doric will give you some hints."
"If you're totally stuck, try just telling him the three items on the Seals."
"The full creed is 'In the Name of the Lever, the Spring and the Winding Key'."

Table of Work Order Hints
hint											used
"You need to find one and pick it up. It's as simple as that."					a number
"Well, it's not quite that simple..."
"The work order belongs to strange Brother Sa'at, who works in the Orrey Room."
"But he'll let you have the work order once it's ready."

Table of Book Hints
hint											used
"You get it from the Library, of course!"							a number
"But the Library doesn't seem to have any shelves. It's got a contraption with cranks and numbers."
"The first thing you need to do is find the code for the book, by using the index."
"Try looking up the book in the card catalogue by the library door."
"You'll need to remember what the book is called!"

Table of Right Numbers Hints
hint											used
"The machine has three cranks."								a number
"Cranks are good for turning."
"But you might have difficulty getting the numbers to move the way you want to. How to change the tens?"
"Read the description of turning the crank carefully."
"You're always turning clockwise (like a good acolyte)."
"What happens if you turn the cranks anticlockwise?"
"Try turning the cranks clockwise and anticlockwise several times, until you get the numbers listed in the card catalogue."

Table of Book-2 Hints
hint											used
"You need to turn the machine on, of course!"						a number
"There's a big chain. Pull!"

Table of Stamp Hints
hint																			used
"He needs to put his seal on it. A seal is a blob of molten wax into which a ring is pressed. It shows who sealed the letter, and that it hasnt been opened by anyone else."	a number
"Luckily, Sa'at will do all of that for you, so long as you can get him some wax."
"Some purple wax, that is."

Table of Wax Hints
hint											used
"A Cathedral is full of wax."									a number
"But it tends to be in a particular form."
"Providing light..."
"There are some candles in the Shrine to the east of the Lower Nave."
"But candles are not quite waxy enough for Sa'at. You'll need to melt them down."

Table of Melting Hints
hint											used
"Look around. Maybe you can find something hot."						a number
"There's a brazier in the Calendar Shrine. Try melting the candles on that."

Table of Wax Lost Hints
hint											used
"If you've melted some candles on the brazier, they'll have turned into pools of wax."		a number
"But you need a tool to get them off the brazier again."
"Have you found a good tool? You might have found one in the Abbey, or you might find one in the Library."
"Try scraping the wax with the knife."

Table of Wax Wrong Hints
hint											used
"You need purple wax. The candles are red, yellow and blue."					a number
"One candle won't be enough."
"You need a way of combining some colours."
"Try putting more than one candle on the brazier at the same time!"
"But which two colours will give you purple?"
"Keep trying combinations or if you get stuck..."
"Red and blue mix to make purple."

Table of Calendar Hints
hint											used
"You can look at it."									a number
"You can be amazed at the power of good clockwork."
"You can even try standing on it."
"But in the end, it's not important to what you're doing here."

Table of Archbishop-2 Hints
hint											used
"The Archbishop is a very important man."							a number
"He's a big cog in the Klockwerk world."
"You are not important. You're a tiny tooth that only gets to intersect with other teeth once in every revolution."
"He won't listen to you. But that won't stop you getting into even worse trouble..."

Table of Figure Hints
hint											used
"You could try catching him."								a number
"Or maybe that's too scary."
"You could just hide and eavesdrop."
"Try listening."

Table of Figure Gone Hints
hint											used
"You'd better get after him!"								a number
"Follow him around the clerestory, then up the secret ladder."

Table of Gargoyles Hints
hint											used
"You need to get over the clock."								a number
"It's too far to jump."
"But there's something that can carry you over."
"Grab the penduluum."
"But you'll have to time it right!"
"Wait, until the penduluum is in the right spot, then grab it."

Table of Lower Gears Hints
hint											used
"There are lots of different ways through the gears."						a number
"You could get completely lost walking around them."
"But which way did the Figure actually go?"
"The Figure scurried away upwards."
"Try examining the gears. There are rungs on them."
"Go up (from anywhere in the Lower Gears!) and you'll be back on track."

Table of Barrel and Chain Hints
hint											used
"If you play around with the crank and the lever, you should be able to work out what it's for."	a number
"The crank is for winding up the massive counterweight of the Cathedral Clock."
"It also winds the chain into the barrel and then, when the lever is released, that chain shoots away upwards."
"Upwards is the way you want to go."
"Try winding the crank, taking hold of the chain, and then pulling the lever."

Table of Which Way Hints
hint											used
"You're trying to keep on Figure's tail."							a number
"If you're not sure which way to go, just try following him."

Table of Break Neck Hints
hint											used
"It's pretty high up and you're doing some pretty dangerous things."				a number
"But don't worry, it's just a game. You can't hurt yourself."
"And you can take your time - but you shouldn't, this is a chase!"

Table of Minute Hand Hints
hint											used
"No, you're not..."										a number
"Just you wait."
"Or if you don't want to wait and you're brave, you could try jumping off."

Table of Figure Where Hints
hint											used
"Keep following him."									a number
"But once you're on the rooftops, he could have gone any way."
"You'll have to explore the area."
"You'll come across him - but you won't catch him quite yet!"

Table of Figure Escaped Hints
hint											used
"Seems impossible, doesn't it?"								a number
"You'll need to explore around and see what you can find."
"That building opposite where the Figure's ornithopter was looks interesting, doesn't it?"
"Try getting across the alleyway."

Table of Alleyway Hints
hint											used
"It's too far to jump."									a number
"You need to make a bridge."
"There's a pile of building debris on the roofs. See anything useful in it?"
"There's a long plank of wood. Try putting that in the notch."
"Still no good? You need something to the weigh the wood down with."

Table of Something Heavy Hints
hint											used
"You need something like a big pile of rocks."						a number
"Or bricks."
"There's a fallen-down chimney on the rooftops."
"Can you get some of the bricks free?"
"You might need a tool to cut away some of the mortar."
"Use the knife again to cut the mortar."
"Then take the pile of bricks and put it on the wooden board, to weigh it down."

Table of Balloon Hints
hint											used
"No, you can't."										a number
"You're going to need to find something else to float the balloon with."
"Did you see anything on the rooftop that might help?"
"A source of hot air, perhaps?"
"There was a narrow chimney - but it's all the way across the alley."

Table of Steam Hints
hint											used
"You need to connect up the chimney and the balloon."					a number
"Have you seen anything you could connect to the chimney?"
"Have another look at the debris where you found the plank."
"There's a length of piping there."
"Put the piping on the chimney."
"But the pipe isn't pointing the right way."
"Have you tried turning it?"
"You need to turn it so it points in the right direction, across the alleyway."
"Try turning it to the southwest."

Table of Pipe Hints
hint											used
"You need something to insulate it with."							a number
"Some kind of material."
"Your rag is probably too small..."
"Try the Figure's tarpaulin sheet."
"Wrap the sheet around the pipe. You should now be able to touch it safely."

Table of Figure Fly Hints
hint											used
"Hard to say. You need to see if you can spot him."						a number
"He's a little far away now, so you need something to help you look."
"Have you found the telescope?"
"Look through it. Can you see him that way?"
"Try turning the telescope to different directions."

Table of Telescope Hints
hint											used
"There's a crank, and a pointer."								a number
"Did you try setting the pointer?"
"And then turning the crank?"
"If you did, then you should have got the telescope to move!"

Table of Giant Hints
hint											used
"This giant is seriously angry about his roof."							a number
"You'd better explain yourself. Try telling him about what's happened to you."
"Tell him about the Figure, for example, or tell him about the Abbot."
"You should find he's not quite as unfriendly as he first appears!"

Table of Diagram Hints
hint											used
"You need to search everywhere you can think of."						a number
"There are a lot of places to look in Covalt's shop."
"Try looking under things, inside things and on things."
"Examine everything!"
"For example, the desk is covered in lots of different things. Examine them all."
"You can also ask Covalt about the various things."
"If you really can't find the diagram..."
"...try looking under the bed."

Table of Thinking Hints
hint											used
"Covalt's very clever, but sometimes clever people have too much going in their heads to find it all."	a number
"You can help Covalt's thinking but only if you can work out what it is he's trying to think about."
"Luckily, he's dropping a lot of clues."
"He wants to think of something different."
"Have you tried asking him about different things?"
"Ask him about something different, literally!"

Table of Address Hints
hint											used
"Go!"											a number
"There's a door to the street in the workshop. Go through it!"

Table of Address-2 Hints
hint											used
"There are guards blocking your way."							a number
"You've got past guards before."
"You need to prove you're meant to be here."
"You've already done this once before."
"Try showing them the work order that you showed to Doric."

Table of Counting House Hints
hint											used
"Your aim is to get to the Difference Engine."							a number
"It's a big machine that takes up most of the building."
"It's through the glass doors to the north..."
"...but you can't go that way, at least, not straight away - there are two women who'll catch you!"
"Maybe there's a way around the back."
"Try going up the stairs and along the corridor."
"You'll find a metal grille. Go through that."

Table of Machine Spotted Hints
hint											used
"Have you found your way to the balcony yet?"						a number
"The two women talking are going to see you if you climb down."
"But they won't be there for very long."
"Wait until they've gone, then climb down."

Table of Abacus Hints
hint											used
"You need a key."										a number
"Brother Horloge's keys aren't going to work. If you're going to find a key around here it'll be, well, around here."
"Have a look around in the engine."
"Examine everything."
"There's a ruby key sticking out of the spindles. Take that, and unlock the abacus with it."

Table of Machine Use Hints
hint											used
"This machine takes questions in the form of five digit numbers, and then answers them."		a number
"You need to set two questions: called the ACTOR and the ACTION."
"You can get a clue to phrase your questions by taking a pamphlet from the box by the giant lever."
"You need to ask where the Figure in Grey has gone. So the ACTOR should indicate the Figure, and the ACTION should indicate where he's going."

Table of Actor Control Hints
hint											used
"As you probably know, words can often have several meanings."				a number
"The pamphlet lists their 'basic' meanings only."
"You'll have to use these as a guide and try to get as close to what you want as you can."

Table of Actor Number Hints
hint											used
"Remember, you're trying to describe the Figure..."						a number
"Try to pick words that describe him."
"He's certainly powerful, wanting, and planning."
"The last two words are the hardest part."
"Remember, you last saw him in an ornithopter. And the thing you know most about him is his colour..."
"The last two dials should be 'flying' and 'cloudy'."
"So the number you want is 11336. Set the abacus to that."

Table of Action Number Hints
hint											used
